+CM_ "ARS510 radar bus (comma harness bus 1), frame-local view. The 0x80 object list and 0x85 metadata record are segmented over many frames and are reassembled in code (ars510.transport); their frames appear here only as raw bytes. Decoded objects are in ars510_objects_vbus.dbc. Documentation: github.com/ds-sebastian/ars510-radar docs/.";
+CM_ BO_ 128 "0x80 object-list transport: a 742-byte record (20 object slots + CRC32) sent every 60 ms as 106 ISO-TP-like frames. First frame starts 12 E4; bytes 1-7 of each frame are appended.";
+CM_ BO_ 133 "0x85 metadata-record transport: a 147-byte record (prefix, ten 12-byte cells, CRC32) sent every 60 ms as 21 frames. First frame starts 10 90.";
+CM_ BO_ 129 "Record-cycle marker: 30 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 within 20 ms after each 0x80 record start.";
+CM_ BO_ 134 "Record-cycle marker: 30 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 within 20 ms after each 0x85 record start.";
+CM_ BO_ 256 "Startup context: word 0 is 0xFFFF in the first frame after power-up, zero afterwards; byte 0 = 0x02 during a PCS alarm.";
+CM_ BO_ 257 "Camera-sent radar-running state: 0x1D while the radar boots, 0x11 once its object list arrives (switches 60 ms before 0x197 bit 8 sets).";
+CM_ BO_ 258 "Sparse state bits 11, 14 and 21.";
+CM_ BO_ 259 "Always zero.";
+CM_ BO_ 384 "Constant CF C0 00 00 00.";
+CM_ BO_ 400 "Radar cycle header (16.7 Hz): number of target summaries, microsecond timestamp and a mod-16 cycle counter.";
+CM_ BO_ 401 "Selected-target companion A (with 0x192): score, age and track code of a target the radar selects itself. Sentinel FE FE FE FC FC FF FE FF = idle.";
+CM_ BO_ 402 "Selected-target summary A (4 bytes): distance and lateral position of one target of the radar's internal tracker, in the object list's encoding. Sentinel 00 FF 00 FF = idle.";
+CM_ BO_ 403 "Selected-target companion B (with 0x194); same layout as 0x191.";
+CM_ BO_ 404 "Selected-target summary B; same layout as 0x192.";
+CM_ BO_ 405 "Event frame, paired with 0x196: exact idle payload on 99.67% of frames; non-idle in a short-time-to-collision state (docs/05).";
+CM_ BO_ 406 "Event frame, paired with 0x195.";
+CM_ BO_ 407 "Startup phase: bit 8 sets once the radar is running and stays set.";
+CM_ BO_ 408 "Constant 0x10.";
+CM_ BO_ 514 "Counter frame: byte 1 high nibble counts mod 16; byte 0 is a check byte that depends only on the counter.";
+CM_ BO_ 528 "Copy of Toyota road-sign-assist data (speed-sign presence, speed-limit value, TSR switch).";
+CM_ BO_ 565 "The radar's ACC target, 50 Hz (content per 60 ms radar cycle): closing speed, relative acceleration, lateral speed and acceleration and the target ID. Position and in-path state are on 0x237.";
+CM_ SG_ 565 REL_SPEED "Closing speed of the ACC target, m/s, negative = closing; 0.125 m/s per code (stopped leads, distance slope).";
+CM_ SG_ 565 REL_ACCEL "Relative acceleration of the ACC target (positive = opening): (code - 100) * 0.125 m/s^2; one code is one speed code per second (closure 1.00 over 2 s windows). Code 100 is the idle value.";
+CM_ SG_ 565 LAT_SPEED "Lateral speed of the ACC target, left positive, about 0.0125 m/s per code (the lateral position changes by 1.2 cm per code-second).";
+CM_ SG_ 565 LAT_ACCEL "Relative lateral acceleration of the ACC target, left positive: (code - 100) * 0.125 m/s^2 (nominal unit, as the longitudinal field). Mostly minus the ego lateral acceleration (-8.2 codes per m/s^2), plus a lateral-speed term; lags the yaw rate.";
+CM_ SG_ 565 TARGET_ID "Target identity: constant while the radar follows one target; 31 with the idle payload. Byte 7 bits 5-7 are 0 with a target, 7 idle.";
+CM_ SG_ 569 STATE "Byte 2 bits 6-7: 1 with an ACC target, 2 idle.";
+CM_ BO_ 567 "The radar's ACC target, 50 Hz: distance, lateral position, in-path state and two tracker bytes (see 0x235).";
+CM_ SG_ 567 LAT_DIST "Lateral position of the ACC target, m, left positive: 12 bits, (code - 2000) * 0.01. One object-list lateral code is 1.5 of these codes (1.499-1.502 on five sets).";
+CM_ SG_ 567 TRACKER_A "Raw tracker byte: 35-36 on a steady target, 44-50 while it accelerates, a median of 48-74 while it brakes.";
+CM_ SG_ 567 TRACKER_B "Raw tracker byte: about 86 for a stopped target, 128-135 for a steady mover, rises toward 240 (and wraps) while the target accelerates or brakes.";
+CM_ SG_ 567 PRESENT "1 with an ACC target.";
+CM_ SG_ 567 IN_PATH "1 while the target is confirmed in the path (level 5).";
+CM_ SG_ 567 IN_PATH_CANDIDATE "1 while the target is a candidate (levels 4-2).";
+CM_ SG_ 567 IN_PATH_LEVEL "In-path level 5, 4, 3, 2; steps to the neighbouring level only; lower levels sit farther from the path.";
+CM_ SG_ 567 LONG_DIST "Distance of the ACC target, 0.025 m per code, zero offset (0.02 m median residual against the 0x680 object range).";
+CM_ BO_ 569 "ACC target, part 3, 50 Hz: target class, object-list flag and the radar cycle clock of the 0x235 / 0x237 content (upstream DBC: TIMESTAMP only).";
+CM_ BO_ 571 "50 Hz companion of the ACC target (3 bytes): CRC-8, counter and the target width in cm.";
+CM_ BO_ 573 "Always zero.";
+CM_ BO_ 576 "Context frame, 16.7 Hz, rolling phase 1-7 in byte 0. At night carries light-source records (two per frame, paired with 0x244); default body by day.";
+CM_ BO_ 577 "Context frame, 16.7 Hz, rolling phase 1-7 in byte 0; default body.";
+CM_ BO_ 580 "Context frame, 16.7 Hz, rolling phase 1-7 in byte 0. At night carries light-source records (two per frame, paired with 0x240); bytes 4 and 7 are always equal.";
+CM_ BO_ 581 "Context frame, 16.7 Hz, rolling phase 1-7 in byte 0; default body.";
+CM_ BO_ 584 "Startup / event context frame with the same rolling phase as 0x240-0x245.";
+CM_ BO_ 589 "State frame: 00 00 00 00 00 00 56 normally; 00 00 00 00 02 00 58 in a rare second state.";
+CM_ BO_ 591 "Startup phase: bit 6 sets once the radar is running.";
+CM_ BO_ 1280 "Constant, unit-specific payload (redacted here; compare your own).";
+CM_ BO_ 1281 "Slow status frame: constants plus a 4-bit state at bit 40.";
+CM_ BO_ 1282 "Slow state frame (every 3 s): two slowly drifting codes (bytes 1 and 2-3) and a unit-specific constant tail (redacted).";
+CM_ BO_ 1664 "One object from the radar's function-level tracker (2 Hz): mostly a stationary roadside object, sometimes a vehicle. Idle payload 00 00 08 00 80 00 80 0A.";
